{"title":"2001 USAMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point in the plane of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> such that the segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/377291318df52e4f013ab2bf28ee82454a9e57da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/9/9f988caff51f7fc88ad40d1d25022c52ffd8f976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e049532148caaf1c48e37658b548a6255c8d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> are the sides of an obtuse triangle. Assume that in this triangle the obtuse angle opposes the side congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/377291318df52e4f013ab2bf28ee82454a9e57da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> is acute.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/3/fb38bb4a5c1b5336d95fa3f1d7449827966624e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB^2+PC^2 &lt; PA^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"152\" height=\"16\" /> and we wish to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7dfa317eefcf43a074761ebac300ac3a24c35864.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB^2 + AC^2 &gt; BC^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"152\" height=\"16\" />.\nIt would be sufficient to prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/0/130788f8cf9a54d97df4b71ffc5d21849aa7cd63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PB^2+PC^2+AB^2+AC^2 \\geq PA^2 + BC^2.\\]\" width=\"331\" height=\"17\" />\nSet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/e/97ef5a3766e3fde52d0b34cb7748c24585b41c2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/c/c6c6e52bfe59cbbbf59139e9f40e0fdb058bfe1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/9/8b90c2d963ad6794060e1af0ec699535f6f4fb59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709e590fce85b64cd13e3dd3f8f9e3d30a1f8ed4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(p,q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />.\nThen, we wish to show\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/4091b210ba7874e6cac3d2e234c464180be08a44.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(p-1)^2 + q^2 + (p-x)^2 + (q-y)^2 + 1 + x^2 + y^2 \\geq p^2 + q^2 + (x-1)^2 + y^2\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/4/b142123b6c3cfa15983b4b5308b139b30e472726.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2p^2 + 2q^2 + 2x^2 + 2y^2 - 2p - 2px - 2qy + 2 \\geq p^2 + q^2 + x^2 + y^2 - 2x + 1\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2ee5139566d8f4cad2a1ca499965da82dd01eef.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p^2 + q^2 + x^2 + y^2 + 2x - 2p - 2px - 2qy + 1 \\geq 0\\]\" width=\"382\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/7/f67738a8776850e58826ab70c121edc9e2e5749e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-p)^2 + (q-y)^2 + 2(x-p) + 1 \\geq 0\\]\" width=\"297\" height=\"19\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/3/e9346175d1bbf1d1c8c5070a2b3ff7013df3cf4c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-p+1)^2 + (q-y)^2 \\geq 0,\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>which is true by the trivial inequality.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the origin. For a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> the vector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/54716282f0245040e8d7bfa6c5044f060629e11e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{AQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"25\" />, and denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/e/f3e0d75c3450ca8f389d08d904ed1fc695734539.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|q|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"18\" /> the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. The given conditions may be written as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d77072780885174c83172e7abcc74ec29e1a644.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|p - b|^2 + |p - c|^2 &lt; |p|^2,\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"19\" />\nor\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/9/7a994c74ed061fdcb0cb68ab014ba12c098d9cad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p\\cdot p + b\\cdot b + c\\cdot c - 2p\\cdot b - 2p\\cdot c &lt; 0.\\]\" width=\"294\" height=\"16\" />\nAdding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d38e96db0115776cb0e2d8de0edd4626dafda6d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2b\\cdot c$\" width=\"38\" height=\"12\" /> on both sides of the last inequality gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/b/48b4a9ccfc31f2e3326f7fba42c8179dae65819c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|p - b - c|^2 &lt; 2b\\cdot c.\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"19\" />\nSince the left-hand side of the last inequality is nonnegative, the right-hand side is positive. Hence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/842cd6280efeb4b90ec6e8d312569691bc97b4a2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos\\angle BAC = \\frac{b\\cdot c}{|b||c|} &gt; 0,\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"42\" />\nthat is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> is acute.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For the sake of contradiction, let's assume to the contrary that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25c483bc280f6dc00407da90d4d1503b2c16051.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = c$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/7/9d78cd4394503dffb3e25f5cd3142ffde2c560fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = a$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/2/f026231bab89dc963b55b720edb00806d18dd581.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA = b$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/0/a6032e9ac7fa3bfe29d9bac5dcafa1b2884f20fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2\\geq b^2 + c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"19\" />. We claim that the quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/3/483ba22e67c264e00ea32fab6c565093bb12cf17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABPC$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is convex. Now applying the generalized Ptolemy's Theorem to the convex quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/3/483ba22e67c264e00ea32fab6c565093bb12cf17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABPC$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/2/5f24972bad4c264b565619c5f6eb9e8e2aae4a71.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\cdot PA\\leq b\\cdot PB + c\\cdot PC\\leq\\sqrt{b^2 + c^2}\\sqrt{PB^2 + PC^2}\\leq a\\sqrt{PB^2 + PC^2},\\]\" width=\"513\" height=\"20\" />\nwhere the second inequality is by Cauchy-Schwarz. This implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/8/5b8e9169dc3aa5a7397a1a5d0726a83b6231cd40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA^2\\leq PB^2 + PC^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"152\" height=\"17\" />, in contradiction with the facts that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/377291318df52e4f013ab2bf28ee82454a9e57da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/9/9f988caff51f7fc88ad40d1d25022c52ffd8f976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e049532148caaf1c48e37658b548a6255c8d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> are the sides of an obtuse triangle and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/d/09d476b826bc7860171a61c0f078c0009c1a4036.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA &gt; \\max\\{PB, PC\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We present two arguments to prove our claim.\n</p><p><i>First argument</i>: Without loss of generality, we may assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are in counterclockwise order. Let lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee61fd6e8a1926a802b97fc99b66b8687d8f620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/6/1d69232050ab0ada641e7e2035f6e7c795795b65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" /> be the perpendicular bisectors of segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee61fd6e8a1926a802b97fc99b66b8687d8f620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/6/1d69232050ab0ada641e7e2035f6e7c795795b65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, the circumcenter of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee61fd6e8a1926a802b97fc99b66b8687d8f620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/6/1d69232050ab0ada641e7e2035f6e7c795795b65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" /> cut the plane into four regions and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is in the interior of one of these regions. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66f14563f1273e35725bb8764c6617aeec3deeb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA &gt; PB$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/d/3ed7216d619d4b595cba0acfb14a6520fcf3c2af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA &gt; PC$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> must be in the interior of the region that opposes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> is not acute, ray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> does not meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee61fd6e8a1926a802b97fc99b66b8687d8f620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" /> and ray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> does not meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/6/1d69232050ab0ada641e7e2035f6e7c795795b65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> must lie in the interiors of the regions adjacent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59b89dd4d8f2bc78023dc71599f39e9d8ac1aaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{R}_X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"15\" /> denote the region containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/2/3528bdaa19ded633dee2887f66f88a19470d790d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{R}_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/7/42704a35088b2bc1e57096abc3a86602a4bbbfd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{R}_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b2a29799d62cb809f4e8f06306002c0c5694b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{R}_P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/b/7db53e2f39ec8f20c803f39d6197bff2986c2db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{R}_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> are the four regions in counterclockwise order. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f531195ef66d5352b3d6627fb0d9ed5554534b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC\\geq 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />, either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> are on opposite sides of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. In either case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> are on opposite sides of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Also, since ray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> does not meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/6/1d69232050ab0ada641e7e2035f6e7c795795b65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" /> and ray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> does not meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee61fd6e8a1926a802b97fc99b66b8687d8f620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b2a29799d62cb809f4e8f06306002c0c5694b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{R}_P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> is entirely in the interior of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are on opposite sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/3/483ba22e67c264e00ea32fab6c565093bb12cf17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABPC$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is convex.\n</p>\n<center><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2001usamo4-1.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/5/57/2001usamo4-1.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"595\" height=\"537\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span></center>\n<p><i>Second argument</i>: Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66f14563f1273e35725bb8764c6617aeec3deeb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA &gt; PB$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/d/3ed7216d619d4b595cba0acfb14a6520fcf3c2af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA &gt; PC$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be inside or on the sides of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e0830febe7535fbbdf19782a978c79c0c9e6cd70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PBC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66f14563f1273e35725bb8764c6617aeec3deeb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA &gt; PB$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/f/c9f44f8bdaf0ed3e52590f3826da66739944779b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABP &gt; \\angle BAP$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"134\" height=\"13\" /> and hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/c/eac00bbee22a61043faf79410f69d0001b3f98f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC\\geq 90^\\circ &gt; \\angle BAP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"185\" height=\"15\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be inside or on the sides of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/9/749df94b914586c0e95acef62f5d4e521d8f946d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BAP$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. Symmetrically, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be inside or on the sides of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/4/6b46d13cd99c1748fbada9584a2fc2a55168d855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CAP$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. Finally, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/f/c9f44f8bdaf0ed3e52590f3826da66739944779b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABP &gt; \\angle BAP$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"134\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/0/ff014012387ed5dcbfe626a987b00d9efdda8c42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACP &gt; \\angle CAP$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"134\" height=\"13\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/4/fe488ed343831b47e9b9482dd76d7f2abb659dee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle ABP + \\angle ACP &gt; \\angle BAC\\geq 90^\\circ\\geq\\angle ABC + \\angle ACB.\\]\" width=\"423\" height=\"15\" />\nTherefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be inside or on the sides of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Since this covers all four cases, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/3/483ba22e67c264e00ea32fab6c565093bb12cf17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABPC$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is convex.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the origin in vector space, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> denote the position vectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/299ddf7c0f03ea46bf09f81f93adeea0756aa15c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" /> respectively. Then the obtuse triangle condition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/1/d818930deb241266dce1246d581e6947fafd687d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA^2 &gt; PB^2 + PC^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"152\" height=\"16\" />, becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/b/7ebe71b5089be62fadd35cca0aadaea7df31e5c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 &gt; b^2 + c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" /> using the fact that the square of a vector (the dot product of itself and itself) is the square of its magnitude. Now, notice that to prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e2c830e136e667485791216de260e10db2c2195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BAC}$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> is acute, it suffices to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/f/56f63d22fef167264b0cf8d9f853377ea2d69b40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a - b)(a - c) &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/a/24a381efe2167058ac81dd6bf7946c3fea69584b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 - ab - ac + bc &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"167\" height=\"16\" />. But this follows from the observation that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c58df014ba89cebc3f40ed0ad7920034b5289f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(-a + b + c)^2 \\ge 0,\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"19\" />\nwhich leads to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/0/b806c6f2a12cd7155fbdcd960a859e195c7fa7ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2a^2 - 2ab - 2ac + 2bc &gt; a^2 + b^2 + c^2 - 2ab - 2ac + 2bc \\ge 0\\]\" width=\"463\" height=\"17\" />\nand therefore our desired conclusion.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec00004a5113b974f70a8e26c3781261e56464e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M, N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> be midpoints of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. For the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/0/a30b517e57d997ca3c772f2799952ed0a38a3c65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, P, C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />; let's apply Euler's quadrilateral formula,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/5/415b5478cb135822685f196332ecf631011dc289.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB^2 + BP^2 + PC^2 + CA^2 = AP^2 + BC^2 + 4MN^2 \\geq AP^2 + BC^2 .\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"18\" />\nGiven that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef4978314e0134713ac286d81bc6f0ff7d717e70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP^2 &gt; BP^2 + PC^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />. Thus,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/a/d8a142da893133e3b89ad735e6f4e0135736ce2e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB^2 + AC^2 &gt; BC^2 .\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"17\" /> \nand we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> is acute.\n</p><p>(Lokman GÖKÇE)\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Without loss of generality, assume that in a Cartesian coordinate system, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is at the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4b86f54134d69cad8793688a431aa907aaf2698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is at the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a306093bbd9e0699c65dba033c9483cd379dc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be at the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/8/c188c32a5e24eac442d148f4580524e150fc202b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b_x,b_y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be at the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/4/b94e82db2cd7e55c5d725e485e398913d3b7ec48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p_x,p_y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" />. Without loss of generality, also assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/2/ce242c905b636a21e0732c5b6ad0f60553dc71a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_y&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"51\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Now, assume for contradiction that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> is not acute. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/377291318df52e4f013ab2bf28ee82454a9e57da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/9/9f988caff51f7fc88ad40d1d25022c52ffd8f976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e049532148caaf1c48e37658b548a6255c8d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> are the sides of an obtuse triangle, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/377291318df52e4f013ab2bf28ee82454a9e57da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> the longest side, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/9/d7978bd5e48191eb83df0d3f7dfa373ee67c5695.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA^2&gt;PB^2+PC^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />, implying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54bcc186debef744dc85624758acdc07e244e677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_x^2+p_y^2&gt;(p_x-b_x)^2+(p_y-b_y)^2+(p_x-1)^2+p_y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"391\" height=\"24\" />. This inequality simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e51e2227780395300d1c67a48a2dabf656933980.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_x^2-2p_x b_x+b_y^2-2p_y b_y+p_x^2-2p_x+1+p_y^2&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"378\" height=\"24\" />. Note that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/4349148e4e075390fa2122ef048cfc2c1274c6a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_x^2-2p_x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a48395f5191db1ec5ad8279f800a9ffd99c39b2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_y^2-2p_y b_y+p_y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"121\" height=\"24\" /> are both perfect squares, all terms of this inequality except for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/7/8a70a4672b424043dfd3219a6905a68ed0dd80f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2p_x b_x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> are already guaranteed to be nonnegative.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/7/687abca8726e55bffad94993181b5e880c9592af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_x&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> would be closer to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> than to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, but since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0a0f064947c2b3825bb0420aec4c8e23a3f949a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA^2=PB^2+PC^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />, this is not possible. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2f28e4febac759afdc6db59b3f5bbe93a14e00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_x \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> not being acute implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/5/e7570160a5e0e6b04562e057d74edc3feeb3f7c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_x \\leq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/1/8c1450e2041bd9f4a39737ab9dd923aa0fe4d706.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2p_x b_x \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" />. But now since all terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e51e2227780395300d1c67a48a2dabf656933980.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_x^2-2p_x b_x+b_y^2-2p_y b_y+p_x^2-2p_x+1+p_y^2&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"378\" height=\"24\" /> are guaranteed to be nonnegative, this entire expression cannot be negative, leading to a contradiction. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> is acute.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>To maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />, we try to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/4/f64cd0f9104ed8209114f939ba5fe63a529a7e28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/1/c311fd04155cec6df4bf9ff0d343334cfe623813.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />, which occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/673ba12ebff0a5d17733fa71ae8a92852f3be041.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB = PA \\sin \\angle PAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"167\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/d/00d3b5c315837737f56fe31224ed3e6e49a332d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PC = PA \\sin \\angle PAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"166\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f19e3233aec68ec68af4928ee5af0ae4b64ab72a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PAB = \\theta_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/6/876ef6cf3d3782b4be9a1b07dfe468726eb7a964.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PAC = \\theta_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/0/ba05abe4e06f756f8a036dfd629595e09bf640d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PC, PB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/377291318df52e4f013ab2bf28ee82454a9e57da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> form an obtuse triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/9/8c9370f669ac84904a8b2fba19e595773e710fc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PC^2 + PB^2 &lt; PA^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>We now have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/5/ab5b6c3cf884d2151d857c092617e2597438c95d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2(\\theta_1) + \\sin^2(\\theta_2) = \\frac{PB^2+PC^2}{PA^2} &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"300\" height=\"41\" />. The premise is now obvious; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/0/2e0a021762071896ef866336800230a85b03df59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2(\\theta_2) &lt; \\cos^2(\\theta_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"22\" />, which means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/f/d2f35dd5c17561bfa765124ad532f2ed0d311c76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta_2 &lt; 90 - \\theta_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"17\" />, so we're done.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO\" title=\"2001 USAMO\">2001 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2001 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2001\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017192401\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.065 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.088 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 935/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 30961/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.691      1 -total\n 61.63%    8.438      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 36.61%    5.013      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7432:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017192401 and revision id 287965. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}